eived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2018-06-14T03:39:56Z","updated_at":"2021-11-29T13:20:13Z","closed_at":"2019-05-20T14:10:17Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nMaven/HttpDownloaders initiate downloads directly into repository cache paths, which, when interrupted, leave invalid repository cache contents that only fail on `get`, and are not re-downloaded.\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\nPerform a build which populates a file in the repository cache for an http archive external repository\r\nModify the `file` content in the repository cache to produce an inconsistent checksum to its cache key value\r\nDelete the root/external/<repository> to ensure an attempted repository fetch\r\nRun a fetch/query/build/test/run which utilizes the external repository\r\nBe greeted with an error message indicating that you should `Please delete the directory ...<cache entry digest> and try again.`\r\n\r\nObserve that this is repeatable\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nUbuntu 16.04\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\nrelease 0.14.0, reproduces with current HEAD","closed_by":{"login":"aehlig","id":9567293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NjcyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9567293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig","html_url":"https://github.com/aehlig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aehlig